# Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy puts every page of this site in its own browsing
# context group: a window it opens cannot reach back through `window.opener`, and
# a cross-origin page that opens one of ours cannot script it. Nothing here uses
# that link. /buy is a same-tab 302 to Stripe (see _redirects), and every link
# that opens a new tab already carries rel="noopener".
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is deliberately NOT set here. Astro builds it per
# page from hashes of that page's own scripts (`security.csp` in
# astro.config.mjs), and one static header for every path cannot know them.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Everything under /_astro/ carries a content hash in its filename, so the URL
# changes whenever the bytes do. Without this, Workers Assets serves them with
# the same `max-age=0, must-revalidate` as the HTML, which puts a conditional
# request on the render-blocking stylesheet on *every* refresh — the round-trip
# that gave the buttons time to paint unstyled. See src/styles/tokens.css.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
